06. INTERFACE STATUS, SPEED, DUPLEX, ERRORS
================================================================================
SW1# show ip interface brief
SW1# show interfaces status
SW1# show interfaces gigabitEthernet 0/1 status
SW1# show interfaces gigabitEthernet 0/1
SW1# show interfaces gigabitEthernet 0/1 counters errors
SW1# show interfaces description
SW1# show interfaces gigabitEthernet 0/1 switchport
SW1# show running-config interface gigabitEthernet 0/1

MANUAL SPEED/DUPLEX (IF SUPPORTED)
---------------------------------
SW1# configure terminal
SW1(config)# interface gigabitEthernet 0/1
SW1(config-if)# speed 1000
SW1(config-if)# duplex full
SW1(config-if)# description UPLINK_TO_SW2
SW1(config-if)# no shutdown
SW1(config-if)# end
SW1# show interfaces gigabitEthernet 0/1

RESTORE AUTO-NEGOTIATION (IF SUPPORTED)
--------------------------------------
SW1(config-if)# speed auto
SW1(config-if)# duplex auto

CAUTION: Not all ports accept manual speed or duplex. Keep settings compatible
         at both ends, and prefer auto-negotiation where supported/recommended.
         'PMN{SPEED_DUPLEX_CONFIGURED}' is not an IOS command (lab feedback).

================================================================================
07. PoE - POWER OVER ETHERNET
================================================================================
SW1# show power inline
SW1# show power inline fastEthernet 0/1
SW1# show power inline gigabitEthernet 0/1
SW1# show power inline police             ! Supported platforms only

CONFIGURE PoE (SUPPORTED PoE SWITCH PORTS ONLY)
-----------------------------------------------
SW1# configure terminal
SW1(config)# interface gigabitEthernet 0/1
SW1(config-if)# power inline auto
SW1(config-if)# end

DISABLE PoE ON ONE PORT (DISRUPTIVE TO POWERED DEVICE)
------------------------------------------------------
SW1(config-if)# power inline never

NOTE: PoE commands do not work on ports/devices lacking PoE hardware.
      'fa0/0' may not exist on common access switches; inspect port names.

