08. IP ADDRESSING / SWITCH MANAGEMENT SVI
================================================================================
LAYER 2 SWITCH MANAGEMENT IP
----------------------------
SW1# configure terminal
SW1(config)# vlan 100
SW1(config-vlan)# exit
SW1(config)# interface vlan 100
SW1(config-if)# ip address 192.168.100.2 255.255.255.0
SW1(config-if)# no shutdown
SW1(config-if)# exit
SW1(config)# ip default-gateway 192.168.100.1
SW1(config)# end
SW1# show ip interface brief

ROUTER INTERFACE
----------------
R1# configure terminal
R1(config)# interface gigabitEthernet 0/0
R1(config-if)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
R1(config-if)# no shutdown
R1(config-if)# end
R1# show ip interface brief

NOTE: For L3 switches with 'ip routing' enabled, use a default route rather
      than relying on 'ip default-gateway'. An SVI may stay down unless its
      VLAN is active with at least one operational forwarding member port.

