14. ACL - BASIC VERIFICATION AND EXAMPLE
================================================================================
R1# show access-lists
R1# show ip access-lists
R1# show running-config | section access-list
R1# show ip interface gigabitEthernet 0/0

EXTENDED ACL EXAMPLE (ONLY ALLOW HTTP TO A TARGET FROM A SUBNET)
---------------------------------------------------------------
R1(config)# ip access-list extended WEB_ONLY
R1(config-ext-nacl)# permit tcp 192.168.10.0 0.0.0.255 host 192.168.20.10 eq 80
R1(config-ext-nacl)# deny ip any any log
R1(config)# interface gigabitEthernet 0/0
R1(config-if)# ip access-group WEB_ONLY in

CAUTION: ACLs have implicit 'deny all' at end. The example will block other
         inbound IP traffic; adapt it before applying to a real network.

